    "created_at": "2021-03-15T15:53:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-15T15:53:58Z",
    "body": "> one thing bz mentions there that null always means empty dictionary, but I'm not sure if that's applicable to a dictionary in a union as well.\r\n\r\nIt is. Note step 3 in <https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#es-union>, where if the JS value is `null` or `undefined`, and the union contains a dictionary type, the JS value gets converted into the dictionary type.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
